    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The station was later renamed Clifton and became a key transfer point for ferry passengers heading to Manhattan's South Ferry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clifton_station_(Staten_Island_Railway)"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The waterfront once buzzed with ship repair yards, warehouses, and factories along Front and Edgewater Streets, but industrial activity waned as shipping moved to New Jersey.",
